course: dictionary
lesson: 6340
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word mouse has three meanings, so context matters. Look at the words around it to find out which one the writer means. The plural of the animal is mice, not mouses. «Owls, foxes, cats, weasels, snakes and hawks all hunt mice.» Here the clue is hunt: mice are animals that get hunted.
explain: A computer mouse is a small tool you move by hand. Mouses is sometimes used for computer mice, but mice is the usual plural. «Click the mouse to open the file» is about a tool, because you click on a screen, not on an animal.
explain: A shy, quiet person can also be called a mouse. The phrase «as quiet as a mouse» uses the animal's quietness to describe someone who says very little. When you meet mouse, ask: which meaning fits here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: A mouse is a very small animal with a long thin tail, round ears and sharp teeth.
fact: The plural of the animal is mice: one mouse, two mice.
fact: A computer mouse is a small tool you move by hand to point and click on a screen.
fact: «A family of barn owls can eat over a thousand mice and voles in a year.» Owls are hunters, and mice are their prey.
fact: «As quiet as a mouse» means very quiet, and a shy person is sometimes called a mouse.
exercise: «Owls, foxes, cats, weasels, snakes and hawks all hunt mice.» In this sentence, what is a mouse? | *A small animal that is hunted | A kind of bird | A shy, quiet person | A tool for pointing at a screen
exercise: Dad says, «Click the mouse to open the file.» Which meaning of mouse is this? | A type of trap | A small animal with a long thin tail | A shy, quiet person | *A small tool you move by hand to point and click
exercise: Mum says, «Ali is as quiet as a mouse in class.» What does this mean? | Ali is a computer | *Ali is very quiet | Ali is hungry | Ali is very loud
test: Which is the plural of the animal mouse? | *Mice | Mouses | Mouse-es | Mouse's
test: In science, what is a mouse? | A bird | *A rodent and a mammal | A fish | A reptile
exam: Which best describes a mouse in the sentence «The barn owl caught a mouse in the field»? | *A small animal with a long tail | A shy, quiet person | A computer tool | A large dog
